    "block": 3,
    "independent_interpretation": "For a positive number, standard form is a*10^n with 1<=a<10 and integer n. Quantity order is n itself, NOT nearest power of ten, NOT 10^n, NOT the exponent in an unnormalized expression. Fractional coefficients must become decimals; repeating decimals can remain repeating or be rounded when necessary. The source fixes no universal rounding precision, so exact equality must not be claimed for a finite rounded expansion and any candidate-required precision must be explicit.",
    "boundary_cases": "1 is allowed; 10 is excluded. Multiplying coefficients across 10 changes n. Values 1.025*10^-5, 4*10^-9 and 1.06*10^10 test normalization rather than reading the printed exponent."
  },
