      "independent_solution": "Domain x!=0. Plot y=6/x (branches in quadrants I and III, axes are asymptotes), and each straight line. a) line y=x-1 has intercept-1, intersection points(-2,-3),(3,2), so roots{-2,3}. Algebraic cross-check x^2-x-6=(x-3)(x+2)=0 confirms both. b) line y=x+3 has intercept3; roots x=(-3±sqrt33)/2≈-4.3722813,1.3722813; intersection ordinates(3±sqrt33)/2≈-1.3722813,4.3722813. Graphical readings at hundredths would be-4.37,1.37 if explicitly requested. Distinct negative and positive branches must be covered; x=0 is not a root.",
